-- s 54(1): a smaller panel only if the Seventh Schedule so provides.
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(1), may my case in the Court of Appeal be heard and decided by this number of Judges` 2 `scja2 seat: yes` `2 Judges`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(1), may my case in the Court of Appeal be heard and decided by this number of Judges` 1 `scja2 seat: yes` `a single Judge or 2 Judges`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(1), may my case in the Court of Appeal be heard and decided by this number of Judges` 3 `scja2 seat: yes` `2 Judges`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(1), may my case in the Court of Appeal be heard and decided by this number of Judges` 1 `scja2 seat: yes` `2 Judges`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the person says the Seventh Schedule does not allow fewer than 3 Judges: the "if" is not met
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(1), may my case in the Court of Appeal be heard and decided by this number of Judges` 2 `scja2 seat: no` `2 Judges`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: the person cannot say what the Schedule provides
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(1), may my case in the Court of Appeal be heard and decided by this number of Judges` 2 `scja2 seat: I am not sure` `2 Judges`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54(2): a Judge must not sit on an application to discharge or vary the Judge's own direction or order.
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(2), may the Judge who made a direction or order in my case sit on my application to discharge or vary it` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(2), may the Judge who made a direction or order in my case sit on my application to discharge or vary it` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54(3): of 3 Judges one falls ill; every party consents, so the 2 remaining carry on.
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(3)(a), must the Court of Appeal carry on and decide my case after some of its Judges can no longer continue` 3 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(3)(b), must my case be reheard after some of the Judges can no longer continue` 3 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- only one Judge remains: the case must be reheard
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(3)(a), must the Court of Appeal carry on and decide my case after some of its Judges can no longer continue` 3 2 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(3)(b), must my case be reheard after some of the Judges can no longer continue` 3 2 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a party does not consent
#ASSERT (`Under section 54(3)(b), must my case be reheard after some of the Judges can no longer continue` 3 1 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 55(1), (3)
#ASSERT (`Under section 55(1), may the Court of Appeal decide my matter without hearing oral arguments` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 55(1), may the Court of Appeal decide my matter without hearing oral arguments` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 55(3), may the Court of Appeal direct that my matter be heard by exchange of written correspondence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 55(3), may the Court of Appeal direct that my matter be heard by exchange of written correspondence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 56(1): summary dismissal on the court's own motion if it is satisfied of any of three things.
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(1), may the Court of Appeal summarily dismiss my appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(1), may the Court of Appeal summarily dismiss my appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(1), may the Court of Appeal summarily dismiss my appeal or application on its own motion` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: the court is not acting on its own motion
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(1), may the Court of Appeal summarily dismiss my appeal or application on its own motion` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 56(2): an opportunity to show cause, and consideration of the representations
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(2), has the Court of Appeal done what it must before summarily dismissing my appeal or application` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(2), has the Court of Appeal done what it must before summarily dismissing my appeal or application` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 56(2), has the Court of Appeal done what it must before summarily dismissing my appeal or application` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 57: an application that may be made to the Court of Appeal or another court must first be made to the other court.
#ASSERT (`Under section 57, must I first make my application to the other court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 57, must I first make my application to the other court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 58(1): in a pending appeal the court may make an incidental direction, an interim order or an order for security for costs.
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(1), may the Court of Appeal make this kind of direction or order in my pending appeal or application` TRUE `s 58(1)(b) an interim order to prevent prejudice to the claims of the parties pending the determination of the pending matter`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(1), may the Court of Appeal make this kind of direction or order in my pending appeal or application` TRUE `s 58(1)(c) an order for security for costs, or for the dismissal of the pending matter for default in furnishing security so ordered`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: another kind of order, or nothing pending
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(1), may the Court of Appeal make this kind of direction or order in my pending appeal or application` TRUE `s 58(1) another direction or order`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(1), may the Court of Appeal make this kind of direction or order in my pending appeal or application` FALSE `s 58(1)(a) a direction or order incidental to the pending matter not involving the decision of the pending matter`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 58(4)(b): an application to vary a single Judge's order may only be made with permission; the decision on permission is final.
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(4)(b), may I apply to vary or discharge a direction or order a single Judge made in my case` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(4)(b), may I apply to vary or discharge a direction or order a single Judge made in my case` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(4)(b), may I apply to vary or discharge a direction or order a single Judge made in my case` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(4)(b), is a Judge's decision to give or refuse me permission to apply to vary or discharge an order final` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 58(4)(b), is a Judge's decision to give or refuse me permission to apply to vary or discharge an order final` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 59(4) and (5): further evidence on appeal.
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(4), may I give further evidence to the Court of Appeal on my appeal` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(4), may I give further evidence to the Court of Appeal on my appeal` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(4), may I give further evidence to the Court of Appeal on my appeal` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- subsection (5) applies: subsection (4) does not decide it
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(4), may I give further evidence to the Court of Appeal on my appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(5), may I give evidence of matters after the decision I am appealing without permission` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(5), may I give evidence of matters after the decision I am appealing without permission` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 59(8) and (9): asking the full panel to rehear
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(8), may I ask the full panel to rehear the arguments on my application to adduce further evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(8), may I ask the full panel to rehear the arguments on my application to adduce further evidence` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(9), am I barred from asking the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence` 2 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(9), am I barred from asking the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence` 5 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(9), am I barred from asking the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence` 2 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the bar: 2 Judges decided and 2 hear the appeal (the 2-2 case), or 3 or more decided
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(9), am I barred from asking the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence` 3 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not barred: a single Judge decided, or 2 decided and 3 hear the appeal
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(9), am I barred from asking the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence` 1 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(9), am I barred from asking the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence` 1 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 59(10): the decision was made on Saturday 1 March 2025; 7 days after that date end on Saturday 8 March 2025
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(10), is my request for the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence in time` (Date 8 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(10), is my request for the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence in time` (Date 9 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 8 March a public holiday and 9 March a Sunday: the last day is Monday 10 March 2025
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(10), is my request for the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence in time` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (LIST Date 8 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(10), is my request for the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence in time` (Date 11 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (LIST Date 8 3 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the judgment or order had already been extracted
#ASSERT (`Under section 59(10), is my request for the full panel to rehear my application to adduce further evidence in time` (Date 3 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60: costs
#ASSERT (`Under section 60, may the Court of Appeal make an order as to the costs of my appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60, may the Court of Appeal make an order as to the costs of my appeal` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 60A(1)(a): a matter tried by the General Division in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction.
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(1), may the Court of Appeal order a new trial of my matter` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(1), may the Court of Appeal order a new trial of my matter` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: a criminal matter is outside the power's scope, and the text has no "only" (ruling (c))
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(1), may the Court of Appeal order a new trial of my matter` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not covered: another court, the Singapore International Commercial Court, or supervisory jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(1), may the Court of Appeal order a new trial of my matter` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(1), may the Court of Appeal order a new trial of my matter` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60A(2) and (3)(a)
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(2), may a new trial be ordered because evidence was wrongly admitted or rejected` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(2), may a new trial be ordered because evidence was wrongly admitted or rejected` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(3)(a), may the Court of Appeal give final judgment for the part of my case that was not affected` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60A(3)(a), may the Court of Appeal give final judgment for the part of my case that was not affected` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60B: an error that does not affect the merits or the jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`Under section 60B, may the Court of Appeal reverse or substantially vary a decision, or order a new trial, because of an error that does not affect the merits` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60B, may the Court of Appeal reverse or substantially vary a decision, or order a new trial, because of an error that does not affect the merits` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60C: no stay unless the court orders one; no intermediate act invalidated unless the court directs
#ASSERT (`Under section 60C(1), does my appeal stop the decision I am appealing from being enforced` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60C(1), does my appeal stop the decision I am appealing from being enforced` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 60C(2), is an act or step taken in my case while the appeal is pending invalidated` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 60C(2), is an act or step taken in my case while the appeal is pending invalidated` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Part 6
-- s 62(2): the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar may exercise the Registrar's powers, subject to Rules of Court.
#ASSERT (`Under section 62(2), may the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar exercise a power of the Registrar in my case` `Deputy Registrar` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 62(2), may the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar exercise a power of the Registrar in my case` `Assistant Registrar` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 62(2), may the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar exercise a power of the Registrar in my case` `Assistant Registrar` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not covered: a clerk
#ASSERT (`Under section 62(2), may the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar exercise a power of the Registrar in my case` Clerk FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 64(1)(a)
#ASSERT (`Under section 64(1)(a), must the Sheriff execute the writ or process the Supreme Court gave to the Sheriff in my case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 64(1)(a), must the Sheriff execute the writ or process the Supreme Court gave to the Sheriff in my case` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 65: "Where in any cause or matter the Sheriff is an interested party, the court may appoint ..."
#ASSERT (`Under section 65, may the court appoint someone to act in the Sheriff's place in my case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 65, may the court appoint someone to act in the Sheriff's place in my case` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 68(2): a commissioner for oaths appointed by the Senate may administer an oath for an affidavit, subject to the limits in the appointment
#ASSERT (`Under section 68(2), may a commissioner for oaths appointed by the Senate do this thing for me` `s 68(2)(c)(ii) administer oaths for taking any affidavit or affirmation` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 68(2), may a commissioner for oaths appointed by the Senate do this thing for me` `s 68(2)(d) take and receive statutory declarations` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 68(2), may a commissioner for oaths appointed by the Senate do this thing for me` `s 68(2)(c)(ii) administer oaths for taking any affidavit or affirmation` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not covered: a thing the list does not name
#ASSERT (`Under section 68(2), may a commissioner for oaths appointed by the Senate do this thing for me` `s 68(2) another thing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 72(1): the Registry is open every day except Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(1), is the Registry of the Supreme Court open on this day` (Date 5 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(1), is the Registry of the Supreme Court open on this day` (Date 3 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(1), is the Registry of the Supreme Court open on this day` (Date 4 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(1), is the Registry of the Supreme Court open on this day` (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 72(2): on a Saturday the Registrar may carry on the business if the Chief Justice directed it or the Registrar thinks it extremely urgent
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(2), may the Registrar carry out the Registry's business for me on this Saturday, Sunday or public holiday` (Date 3 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(2), may the Registrar carry out the Registry's business for me on this Saturday, Sunday or public holiday` (Date 3 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(2), may the Registrar carry out the Registry's business for me on this Saturday, Sunday or public holiday` (Date 3 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: an ordinary Monday
#ASSERT (`Under section 72(2), may the Registrar carry out the Registry's business for me on this Saturday, Sunday or public holiday` (Date 5 1 2026) (LIST Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ============================================================
-- scja3: this part's cases seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- scja3-cases-seat.l4: cases for the seat layer.  Expected values are written from the text of the Act (the provision named in each question), beside each assertion,
-- and not from the module's output.  The first case of a question is the case the provision answers JUST TRUE (or its named result); the next is the case that goes the other way
-- or falls outside the provision.

§ `Cases: the seat layer`


-- ---- The Registrar's list of touts (s 73) ----
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(1), can the Registrar put my name on the list of touts` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(1), can the Registrar put my name on the list of touts` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(3), must my name stay off the list of touts for now` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(3), must my name stay off the list of touts for now` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(3), must my name stay off the list of touts for now` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(2), can the Registrar bar me from the precincts of the Supreme Court` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(2), can the Registrar bar me from the precincts of the Supreme Court` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(2), can the Registrar bar me from the precincts of the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(2), must I be allowed to remain in the precincts of the Supreme Court for such time as is necessary` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(2), must I be allowed to remain in the precincts of the Supreme Court for such time as is necessary` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(4), can I appeal to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(4), can I appeal to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(5), can I appeal further from the Judge's decision` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(5), can I appeal further from the Judge's decision` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(7), is my name treated as included in the list under this Act because it appears in another list of touts` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73(7), is my name treated as included in the list under this Act because it appears in another list of touts` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- Measures against unmeritorious or vexatious proceedings (ss 73A to 73D and 74) ----
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(2), can the court stay the legal proceedings I am conducting` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(2), can the court stay the legal proceedings I am conducting` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(2), can the court stay the legal proceedings I am conducting` `scja3 the Family Division of the High Court` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(3), can the court order that I file no further documents in the legal proceedings` `scja3 the Appellate Division` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(3), can the court order that I file no further documents in the legal proceedings` `scja3 the Appellate Division` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(5), can the General Division stay the legal proceedings I am conducting in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(5), can the General Division stay the legal proceedings I am conducting in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(5), can the General Division stay the legal proceedings I am conducting in a subordinate court` `scja3 the Court of Appeal` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(6), can the General Division order that I file no further documents in the legal proceedings in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(6), can the General Division order that I file no further documents in the legal proceedings in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(7), can the court make the order against me` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(7), can the court make the order against me` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(7), can the court make the order against me` `scja3 the General Division` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(8), can the General Division make the order against me in respect of legal proceedings in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(8), can the General Division make the order against me in respect of legal proceedings in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(8), can the General Division make the order against me in respect of legal proceedings in a subordinate court` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the General Division's order` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE `scja3 the Appellate Division as the appeal court`) EQUALS JUST `Appellate Division`
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the General Division's order` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE `scja3 the Court of Appeal as the appeal court`) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the General Division's order` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE `scja3 I do not know which appeal court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9), can I appeal against the General Division's order without permission` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9), can I appeal against the General Division's order without permission` `scja3 the General Division` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9A), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the Appellate Division's order` `scja3 the Appellate Division` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(9A), to which court must I apply for permission to appeal against the Appellate Division's order` `scja3 the General Division` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(10), is this thing within "legal proceedings" for sections 73A, 73B and 73C` `s 73A(10) action` `a civil proceeding`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73A(10), is this thing within "legal proceedings" for sections 73A, 73B and 73C` `s 73A(10) action` `a criminal proceeding`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`Under section 73B(1), can the court make a limited civil restraint order against me` `scja3 the General Division` 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73B(1), can the court make a limited civil restraint order against me` `scja3 the General Division` 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`Under section 73B(1), can the court make a limited civil restraint order against me` `scja3 another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
